{"city": "katsina", "venueId": "central-mosque-katsina", "brief": {"venueId": "central-mosque-katsina", "city": "katsina", "name": "Central Mosque (Katsina)", "archetype": "mosque-sahelian", "subject": "The Katsina Central Mosque in the old city near the Gobarau Minaret: a large Hausa-style prayer hall with a tapering minaret and a walled courtyard (typed)", "form": {"footprint": "rect", "width_m": 55, "depth_m": 40, "storeys": 2, "height_m": 14, "roof": "flat", "wings": 1}, "facade": {"material": "painted-render", "accent": "mud-render", "colours": ["#e8dfc8", "#b98a5e", "#f7f4ee"], "roofColour": "#a8a29a", "roofMaterial": "concrete", "windows": "arched", "windowRatio": 0.2}, "features": [{"id": "minaret", "count": 1, "note": "tapering"}, {"id": "pinnacles", "count": 4, "note": "corner pinnacles"}, {"id": "toron-beams", "count": 1}, {"id": "courtyard", "count": 1}, {"id": "arches", "count": 1}, {"id": "fence-wall", "count": 1}], "setting": {"ground": "laterite", "trees": "acacia", "forecourt": "plaza"}, "style": "sahelian", "era": "19th century core, modernised", "confidence": "low", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Gobarau-Minaret", "what": "Katsina central mosque tradition: the old Gobarau mosque was succeeded in the early 19th century by a new central mosque built by Sarkin Katsina Ummarun Dallaji (1805-1835), probably the current one"}, {"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hausa_architecture", "what": "Hausa mosque: prayer hall + walled courtyard, mud/thatch/tin roof"}], "notes": "Search results say the current central mosque probably dates from Ummarun Dallaji (1805-35) but give no physical description, and it may have been rebuilt in concrete. Form and colours typed from Hausa mosque conventions. Venue scene variant is mosque."}, "style": {"schema": "allworld-city-style", "version": 1, "city": "katsina", "climate": "sahel", "vernacular": "Old walled Hausa city of mud-brick (tubali) and laterite-render compounds in earth ochre and tan, e